   299	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   300	    """
   301	    Expand the seed-marked figure and every cascade-activated figure by stamping each figure's own black-cell complement.
   302	
   303	    Input structure:
   304	    - Black background with 5-6 separated 4-connected figures, each fitting exactly in a 3x3 bbox.
   305	    - Every figure has a unique body color from 1-6; exactly one figure also contains an orange center pixel marking the seed.
   306	    - Each 3x3 bbox contains both foreground cells and black cells, so every figure has a non-empty complement mask.
   307	
   308	    Rule:
   309	    - Treat the orange seed pixel as part of its figure's body color.
   310	    - For any processed figure, compute the 3x3 complement mask of black cells inside that figure's bbox.
   311	    - Build a centered 9x9 stamp region: every foreground cell of the 3x3 figure selects one 3x3 block, and that block is filled by the complement mask in the figure's body color.
   312	    - Any unactivated figure whose 3x3 bbox is touched by at least one stamped cell becomes activated; process newly activated figures round by round, using scan order within each round.
   313	    - Output only the stamped expansions of activated figures; figures never activated are recolored in place to maroon. Later processed stamps overwrite earlier ones.
   314	
   315	    Key insight:
   316	    - A figure's local geometry controls both what gets stamped and which neighboring bboxes are reached, so activation depends on the complement mask itself rather than on distance alone.
